Your client (landlord): Mr Martin Kell

We act for Mr Warsame, the tenant of the above property, which you manage on behalf of your client. This letter is sent under the Pre-Action Protocol for Housing Conditions Claims (England).

Our client reported water coming through the bedroom ceiling on 28 July 2026. Despite your contractor attending on 4 August, the roof has not been repaired. Our client's bedroom ceiling is stained and damp, the room has a persistent smell of damp, and our client has had to sleep in the living room on wet nights. Clothing and a mattress have been damaged.

We ask that within 20 working days of receipt of this letter you:

1. confirm that your client admits liability for the disrepair;
2. provide copies of all documents relating to the condition of the property and repairs since 1 July 2026, including reports, quotes and correspondence with your client;
3. confirm the date on which the roof will be repaired.

We would also invite your client to put forward an offer of compensation. Our client would accept £2,500 if confirmed within 14 days.

Please do not contact our client about this claim directly. Contact with our client to arrange access for repairs may continue as normal.

